#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Example 3: Graph 3-coloring (Max-3-Cut) {#example-3-graph-3-coloring-"
"max-3-cut}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Max-$k$-Cut problem partitions the vertices of a graph into $k$ groups "
"to maximize the number of edges whose endpoints belong to different groups. "
"For $k = 3$ this is equivalent to finding a 3-coloring that maximizes cross-"
"color edges.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Formally, assign each node $i \\in V$ to one of $k$ groups with binary "
"variables $x_{i,c}$ for color $c \\in \\{1, \\ldots, k\\}$. The one-hot "
"constraint $\\sum_c x_{i,c} = 1$ for each node enforces a unique assignment."
" The objective maximizes cross-group edges:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\min \\sum_{(u,v) \\in E} \\sum_c x_{u,c} \\, x_{v,c}\\\\\n"
"\\text{s.t.} \\sum_{c} x_{i,c} = 1 \\quad \\forall i \\in  V\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The one-hot constraints are ideal for XY-mixers, which the optimizer handles"
" natively.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
